Z||000008||Monkeyman||09-20-2001||09:51 PM||||That would be fierosound (1<sup>st</sup> poster in this thread--other than me).  Awesome stereo setup.  I plan on imitating his sub box to a certain extent.  I wish I could think of another place for the stereo.  Now I'm beginning to wonder about heat/circulation if I still decide to high mount my stereo.||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||09-20-2001||10:15 PM||||Just a thought I had once maybe MM. Make the center console armrest 3" higher and mount a stereo unit where the cigarett lighter is now. Haven't put a 3" block on the console yet to see how it would feel.<P>PS. Email me your phone number again Dave. I have had address book and email problems. Can't find your number for some reason.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||09-20-2001||10:26 PM||||slammed, do you have any model no. info for that? i've had a pioneer indash changer for a while that i want to use but that means the head unit has to go somewhere else. i been looking in all the pioneer catalogs i can find to see if they make something like that. <P>or if anyone knows any possible way an alpine head can control a pioneer changer, i'd like to know.i have an old alpine head with a remote face (wired). i've always heard that a few manufacturers pieces will work with others but it's not real common knowledge so it's hard to know what will. <P>i've heard of wiring the face to the head too. a while back there was even someone who took the face apart, wired the controls to a pontiac steering wheel and put the head unit display in the rear view mirror (scratched away some of the mirror silver and made the display part of the mirror). tricky. i'd like to try it but i'd hate risking a good head unit for experimentation. <P>oh yeah. i also got a underdash mounting kit (essentialy a plastic box that will hold a din unit) that i think might work as the start of a overhead radio holder. look for one from metra. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
